# Nova service identity (fixed, in the preferred 0..199 packaged
# range): user nova UID 167, primary group nova GID 167.
# OpenStack services own the 164-170 block (164 keystone, 165 glance,
# 166 placement, 167 nova, 168-170 neutron/cinder/horizon). Required
# by the shipped service units (systemd User=nova, OpenRC
# command_user nova:nova), nova-manage and the state/log
# directories. UID 167 is not reused by any other packaged identity.
# Supplementary libvirt membership: with polkit disabled, the Unix
# socket group is the only client gate (libvirtd.conf sets
# unix_sock_{ro,rw}_perms 0770 owned by group libvirt), and
# nova-compute speaks to the modular daemons over those sockets.
# Needs the supplementary-groups grammar on install targets
# (baselayout r51+); install refuses loudly otherwise, never silently.
user nova 167 nova /var/lib/nova /sbin/nologin libvirt
group nova 167
dir /var/lib/nova 0750 nova nova
dir /var/log/nova 0750 nova nova
